// Site-level add-to-cart floor for the weekly GA4 funnel diagnosis.
//
// This was an inline literal, numerically identical to
// DIAGNOSIS_THRESHOLDS.working_add_to_cart_rate but applied to a completely
// different metric: this one judges GA4Weekly.atc_rate (sessions that added to
// cart), the other judges GA4ProductWeekly.view_to_cart_rate (PDP views that
// added to cart). Landmine #4 is about the second. Leaving them as two unrelated
// 0.08s meant that fixing Landmine #4 by lowering the constant would silently
// change what `diagnosisTrust` believed the funnel diagnosis was using.
//
// Measured 2026-09-08 against 17 live weeks: the store's median site-level ATC is
// 8.71% and it cleared 8% in 11 of 17 weeks, so this floor is well calibrated for
// this shop. That is NOT true of the product-level constant.
const GA4_LOW_ATC_RATE = 0.08;

